caption: One tiddler for the document, one per item
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/recipes/document-record
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

An e-reader exports a book's highlights as one document: the book's
details at the top, the highlights in an array.  Two kinds of tiddler
want making from it — one for the book, one per highlight — and a
profile makes one kind.  So, two profiles over the same JSON.

```
{
  "title": "The Book's Title",
  "author": "The Book's Author",
  "md5sum": "a1ea75e3…",
  "created_on": 1792408448,
  "entries": [
    { "text": "Highlighted text", "page": 31, "chapter": "2", "time": 1791384732 },
    …
  ]
}
```

''The book'' — a records path of `{{}}`, the document itself, which is
one record:

```
{
  "records": "{{}}",
  "tw-fields": {
    "title":   "book-{{md5sum}}",
    "tags":    "book",
    "caption": "{{author}} - {{title}}",
    "created": "{{created_on|timestamp-to-date}}"
  },
  "custom-fields": {
    "md5sum":     "{{md5sum}}",
    "highlights": "{{entries|pluck[text]}}"
  }
}
```

''The highlights'' — one per entry, each linking back to the book
through `..`, which reaches the document from inside the array:

```
{
  "records": "{{entries[*]}}",
  "tw-fields": {
    "title":   "{{../title}} — p. {{page|zero-pad[3]}}",
    "tags":    "highlight",
    "text":    "{{text}}",
    "created": "{{time|timestamp-to-date}}"
  },
  "custom-fields": {
    "book":    "book-{{../md5sum}}",
    "page":    "{{page}}",
    "chapter": "{{chapter}}"
  }
}
```

Run the book profile first, then the highlights profile, over the same
pasted JSON — or generate an importer from each and run both.  The
`book` field on every highlight points at the book tiddler's title, so
a `<$list filter="[book<currentTiddler>]">` on the book lists its
highlights.
